      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"Subtle inconsistencies\" in the lead pigment sounds a bit concerning for a piece with this kind of valuation. If the board sees \"inconsistent pigment readings\" in the report, they might pull the lot entirely to avoid a scandal. \n\nCan you be more specific? Is there a technical way to explain those readings that wouldn't compromise the attribution? We really need to know if we're looking at a genuine masterwork with some heavy-handed cleaning, or something much worse.",
