      "content": "The discrepancy in the lead pigment readings is largely due to variations in the sample's porosity, potentially indicating areas where the varnish has been stripped or has lifted over the years, exposing underlying layers. This is a common issue in 17th-century etchings and uses of white lead, as the compound can be highly unstable and prone to degradation. If the cleaning or restoration is competent, these variations shouldn't compromise the attribution of the piece as a genuine work by the attributed artist.",
